Fuzz corpora
============

Each corpus directory holds libFuzzer inputs: one file = one test case.

Only hand-written seeds (descriptive names like hostile_*.bin, valid_*.bin)
are version-controlled — they are intentional regression tests for known
crash shapes. Auto-generated coverage artifacts (SHA-named files) are
gitignored: they regenerate during any fuzzing run and are machine-specific.

If a fuzzer finds a crash, promote the input: give it a descriptive name,
add it to the corpus directory, and commit it as a regression seed.
